## Claim
Text: "Commission on Human Rights (CHR) Chairman Chito Gascon called a “surprise military attack” by the Philippine Army,  conducted on members of the New People’s Army (NPA) a “violation of human rights.”"
Claim author: Pinoy News Center
Claim date: October 14, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Was Chito Gascon serving as the Chairman of the Commission on Human Rights (CHR) of the Philippines in October 2020?
Answer: Yes, Chito Gascon was serving as the Chairman of the Commission on Human Rights (CHR) of the Philippines in October 2020. According to the search result, Gascon was CHR Chairman during the 2017 budget deliberations and was quoted as saying he would "hold [his position] until May 2022," meaning he was still in office in October 2020.

Source URL: https://www.rappler.com/newsbreak/inside-track/181966-chr-bigger-2018-budget-chito-gascon-resign-pantaleon-alvarez/

### What was the specific date, location, and context of the military attack referenced in the claim?
Answer: Based on thesearch result, the military attack occurred on a Monday (around 11:20 a.m.) in **Sitio Coloconto, Barangay Bulsa, San Juan, Batangas**, when troops of the 1st Infantry Battalion "clashed with members of the New People's Army (NPA)" while conducting combat operations. The context was that the military operation followed "reports from concerned citizens that a group of NPA terrorists would conduct harassment on the Bulsa detachment," leading to nearly an hour of firefight. However, the search result does not specify the exact calendar date (month/year) of the incident.

Source URL: https://www.pna.gov.ph/articles/1043164

### Were the individuals targeted in the attack confirmed to be members of the New People's Army (NPA)?
Answer: Based on the search result, the report is solely sourced from the Philippine Army (specifically the 1st Infantry Battalion and 2nd Infantry Division), which claimed the individuals were NPA members, describing them as "more or less 15 NPA rebels under alias 'Salma'." The only "confirmation" of their NPA membership comes from the military itself — there is no independent verification cited in the source. The fact that CHR Chairman Gascon characterized the incident as a "surprise military attack" and a "violation of human rights" suggests his concern included the question of whether those targeted were actually confirmed combatants or civilians.

Source URL: https://www.pna.gov.ph/articles/1043164

### How many casualties or affected individuals resulted from the attack, and were they verified as NPA members?
Answer: The search result does not provide specific casualty numbers, only stating that "the rebels brought along their wounded comrades as they fled the area." The encounter involved "more or less 15 NPA rebels" identified by the military under alias 'Salma,' but their NPA membership was based solely on military claims and not independently verified in this source.

